    to the nearest 25% step, never below 100% (1440 lines 125%, 1824 175%,
    2160 200%; 300-400% listed where recommended). Until the user picks one
    the scale is the recommended one, and follows the screen: --set metrics
    (sign-in) and --set desktop (the screen changed) set it, and --set scale
    auto; a pick other than the recommended one sticks (Software\Stained
    Glass\Display ScaleChosen), picking the recommended one again makes it
    automatic, and a scale set before this is kept as the user's. The title
    bars' screen scale (Scale8) is taken from the screen's height at the
    display scale, so Wine does not scale them twice (40 px of 1824 at 175%,
    the share of the screen 1080p's have). effects.conf gives the compositor
    the sizes in the screen's pixels, the taskbar's height and the pointer's
    size. At 1080p and smaller nothing changes. Test: test/hidpi-check.sh
    (mutants SG_MUTANT_SCALE_RECOMMEND_100, SG_MUTANT_SCALE_NO_STICK,
    SG_MUTANT_TITLE_DOUBLE_SCALE, SG_MUTANT_CONF_UNSCALED).

