sg-shell (0.1.0-117) unstable; urgency=medium

  * SG Store offers the Visual Basic 6 runtime (MSVBVM60.DLL; David
    2026-10-05: Meedio's plug-ins General_RemovableInsert and
    General_HideTaskbar need it, and Wine does not have it). Microsoft
    offers it now only inside its own XP Service Pack 3 package (332 MB):
    the new install type cab-dll finds that package's cabinet, takes the
    one file out (and out of its one-file .dl_ cabinet), and as an
    administrator, under one consent, puts it in the 32-bit system
    folder, registers it and writes an Uninstall entry, so the store sees
    it installed. Nothing of Microsoft's is shipped: the user's machine
    downloads it from Microsoft, checked by its SHA-256.
  * A runtime's page has no Open (nothing to open); its Uninstall runs as
    an administrator. A pinned app's page shows the catalogue's licence,
    site and whole description; sg-store --page ID opens on an app's page.
    The page's facts no longer clip their last letter.
  * sg-notify: when a program needs a runtime the store offers and it is
    missing (wine-sg 0817 names it under HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\
    Runtimes\Missing), it asks, once a session, "<program> needs the
    Visual Basic 6 runtime ... Install it from SG Store?" -- Yes opens SG
    Store on its page (Store\Runtimes maps the DLL to the app).
  * Gates: store-check H3 (a stand-in package and runtime DLL; installed,
    registered, detected, --page with licence and no Open, Uninstall;
    mutant SG_MUTANT_NOCABDLL); notify-check: the question, Yes ->
