      and scaled with an area average, cached per person for a month
      (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Stained Glass\Store\Icons). We ship no maker's
      artwork; offline, the letter badge stays.
    - No app is listed twice: a Windows program whose entry names its
      Linux build (Linux=Lnn; 29 pairs: GIMP, OBS, VLC, LibreOffice...) is
      one card with a Linux app / Windows program drop-down. The Linux
      build is suggested unless the entry says Prefer=windows (BleachBit;
      browsers that need Windows sign-on); the build that is installed is
      the card's.
    - Install on several apps queues them, one at a time, in the order
      asked; a waiting one can be cancelled. Uninstall goes through the
      same queue.
    - Uninstall for Windows programs too: the Uninstall entry's
      QuietUninstallString (else UninstallString; MsiExec /I becomes /X),
      as an administrator when the uninstaller asks; --uninstall ID works
      for them.
    - The window looks at what is installed again when it comes forward;
      dpkg's status is read again only when it changes.
    - DYMO Connect and DYMO Label added.
    Test: store-check section L (mutants NOPAIR, NOICON, NOQUEUE, NOQUIET).
  * SG Store: Uninstall. An installed system package -- SG Office, a Linux
    app -- has Uninstall beside Open (it could only be installed: neither
    the Store nor Programs and Features could remove it). After a question,
    the same consent as an install, and sg-admind's new apt-remove: apt-get
