      sg-store64.exe --open ID does the same without the window. Test:
      test/store-check.sh (mutant NOLAUNCH).
    - SG Office from the store on a machine without the sg-office package
      said "SG Office was installed; restart, then install it again to
      finish" -- every time. sg-admind (package-install) registers the
      package with "wine reg import" as the machine account, but its
      service had a private /tmp, which hid the shared wineserver's socket
      (/tmp/.wine-sg-*): the import started a second wineserver of its own,
      so the running one never had sg-office-setup.exe's App Paths (the
      store's elevated copy stopped with 21), and the running one's next
      save dropped the key from system.reg while the import's stamp kept
      the next boot from importing it again. sg-admind.service no longer
      has PrivateTmp (its own files are in /var/tmp and /run). Seen on a
      test machine: the key in system.reg at 23:45:43, gone at 23:45:58,
      never in the running registry; with the unit changed, package-install
      took 2 s and the store went on to SG Office's setup. Test:
      test/admind-check.sh (mutant PRIVATETMP: the old unit).
    - SumatraPDF, installed from the store, was not in Start: it puts its
      shortcut at the top of the Start Menu folder, beside Programs, where
      Start did not look. Start now lists shortcuts there too (the user's
      and all users'). Test: test/start-check.sh (mutant NOSTARTROOT, run
      with SG_START_EXE=<a build with -DSG_MUTANT_NOSTARTROOT>).
    - foobar2000 and Mp3tag said "Installed." but stayed "Install": their
      manifests say ElevationRequirement: elevationRequired, which the store
      ignored, so their installers ran as the user -- the files reached
      Program Files, the Uninstall entry (HKLM) did not, and the store (and
      Apps & features) never saw them. Such an installer is now started as
      an administrator (the consent prompt), as winget does. Test:
      test/store-check.sh (mutant NOELEVATE);
      test/browser-manifest-test.c.

