sg-shell (0.1.0-80) unstable; urgency=medium

  * SG Store installs SG Office again (David, on real hardware: "SG Office
    fails to install from the Store"). Three causes, all fixed:
    - The store runs Get SG Office by its App Paths name,
      sg-office-setup.exe, which sg-office never registered: SG Office could
      not install from the store on any machine. office/gen-reg.py registers
      it now, and test/office-check.sh checks that every setup program the
      store names is registered and packaged.
    - A machine made before sg-office was in the image, and only updated
      since, has the store's entry but not the package (updates upgrade;
      they install nothing new). The store now asks for elevation, and the
      elevated copy has sg-admind install the package -- package-install, a
      fixed list of our own packages -- and import its registry defaults as
      the machine account; then Get SG Office runs as before. (Two consent
      prompts in this case, one for the package and one for LibreOffice's
      installer: downloading as SYSTEM breaks off in wine-sg, reported
      separately, so the download stays the person's.)
    - An App Paths entry whose program is gone (a removed package leaves its
      keys) counted as installed; now it does not.
    The catalogue links the entry to its package ("Package"="sg-office").
    Gates: test/store-check.sh (a missing package installed through
    sg-admind in its test mode, a stale App Paths entry ignored, a package
    not on the list refused, mutant NOPACKAGE caught), test/admind-check.sh
    (package-install), test/office-check.sh (the registration). Verified on
    qa3: Store > SG Office > Install, with and without the package.

  * SG Store v2 (David's report, 2026-09-30):
    - The Windows GIMP installed no longer makes the Linux GIMP look
      installed: a Linux app is detected by dpkg's state of its package
      only, a Windows program by its own Uninstall name only -- as a whole
      word ("Git" is not "GitHub Desktop"), with exclusions ("XnView" is
      not "XnView MP") and * for any run of characters.
    - Search: a search box over the whole catalogue (names, makers,
      descriptions, categories); categories to pick from; the keyboard
      (typing searches, Down/Up move through the list, Enter installs or
      opens, Esc goes back to the search box, Ctrl+F).
